{
  "doc": "M3-C07-02 greybox, moved on to env-art's Tamsule Bell kit (M3-C07-1211, ADR 0200: the kit's arena frame, tools/act1/ch07_tamsule_bell_dressing.py; the galleries are the west, Oruvel's, the rim is Oruvel's prow, the moorings at azimuth 325, on the party's side). It was a STAND-IN for the story's side of the Tamsule Bell (act1_ch07.md B04, B05, B07, B09; N-12's sphere form). The real arena, ch07/tamsule_bell (the drop, the play space), is env-art's and the Reefball agent's; this zone stages only the story beats around the match: the stilt galleries (the third gallery, south, where the party sits), the catch-pool and its rim stones (centre) under the weeping column, the Bell and its drop overhead (out of reach, still), a salt-glass panel (north) looking out to the river moorings where Kerrid stands knee-deep, back to the Bell, and Oruvel's empty moorings under the Bell's skirt on the river side (east): six iron rings in a timber staging. The pool is a stand-in floor: there is no swimming in the greybox, so Rhen's place 'in the water' is the rim. Shot ids are the beat sheet's R01-R09 proposals plus R01A (Asha's close inside R01's axis) and R02K (R02's reverse through the salt-glass, Kerrid's cutaway).",
